{
  "meta": {
    "test": "VideoMAE future-tubelet masked reconstruction coherence (analog to V-JEPA's future-tubelet feature-prediction coherence test)",
    "IMPORTANT_CAVEAT": "This is NOT numerically comparable to V-JEPA's predictor-vs-naive cosine scores in vjepa2_base_predictive_coherence.json. V-JEPA's predictor operates in LEARNED FEATURE space (predicting the encoder's own 1024-d representation of the target tubelet). VideoMAE's decoder operates in NORMALIZED PIXEL-PATCH space (predicting per-patch mean/var-normalized RGB values, its native MSE pretraining target). The two 'predictor_score' numbers below are on different scales measuring different things and must not be reported as a single unified predictive-coherence ranking. This test is reported as a separate, video-native reconstruction- coherence result, addressing the reviewer's point that a genuine video-native self-supervised objective exists for VideoMAE even though it is not the same objective as V-JEPA's.",
